    LLM: 'Game: Laus (BÃ¶se Dame). Avoidance trick-taking. 32-card deck (A-7). 3-4 players. Must follow suit. Queen of Spades = 50 pts, A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2. Can play Qâ™  when void in led suit. Lowest score when someone reaches 100 wins.',
    Player: "Welcome to Lausâ€”the 'Louse' game! Avoid the Queen of Spades at all costsâ€”she's worth 50 penalty points! Follow suit, void your weak suits early, and dump high cards on your opponents. Lowest score wins when someone hits 100!",
    objective: 'Score the fewest points. Avoid capturing the Queen of Spades (50 points) and minimize capture of other point cards.',
    gameplay: 'Standard trick-taking: 1. Must follow suit if possible. 2. If void in led suit, may play any card. 3. Highest card of the led suit wins the trick. 4. There are no trumps. 5. Winner leads to the next trick.',
